Canonical Retained-Document Streaming — S7B
===============================================================================

Status: B1-B5 implemented; final qualification and B6 closeout remain open.
The public DocumentStream lifecycle retains canonical grammar, source, events,
diagnostics, and completed typed nodes. Ordinary publication shares persistent
journals; explicit finite previews and final exports have separate accounting.
Baseline: S7A PR #825, 34cb58ad3e676723d7161ae52906395cdfaa83c0.
Branch: codex/syntax-s7b-streaming, targeting codex/syntax-s7-document-root.

1. Ownership and scope
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

S7A completes document recognition, rule-owned recovery, typed consumers, existing
semantics, and correct edits. S7B retains parsing state as source arrives. S8
switches production consumers and removes the retiring paths. S7A obligations
stay on S7A; beginning this draft does not certify its base as complete.

One canonical grammar, recognition/recovery implementation, and typed syntax
model remain authoritative. Shared execution changes belong in the S7B diff;
S2/S3 remain frozen. Inventory coverage remains 520/539: no productions added.
No new semantics, FSM scheduling, runtime activation, production caller switch,
compatibility AST, parser library, streaming grammar, or legacy fallback.
Production machinery stays safe, deterministic, platform independent core/alloc;
I/O, transports, clocks, threads, and async scheduling remain external.

This is retained-document streaming, not constant-memory consumption. Accepted
source and syntax remain inspectable. Historical snapshots retained by callers
are counted separately from the active session's storage.

2. Lifecycle and API responsibilities
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Open -> Finishing -> Finished
Open/Finishing -> Cancelled
Open/Finishing -> Limited (explicit hard-resource outcome)

Start owns document identity, parser configuration, hard limits, and counters.
Append accepts valid UTF-8 text without final EOF. It reports accepted bytes,
progress, and compact syntax/diagnostic changes. Advance processes accepted input
under a caller-provided work allowance. NeedInput and NeedsProcessing are distinct
from syntax errors and hard limits. Empty append changes no revision or counters.

Finish declares final EOF once; advance may drain its pending bounded work.
Repeated finish preserves the same completion state/result and does not repeat
work. Finished/cancelled/limited streams reject appends with defined API errors.
Cancel stops processing, retains accepted source, and never implies final EOF.
When an append exceeds retained-source capacity, reject that append atomically;
previously accepted source remains available. Other hard limits preserve every
accepted byte, including the unparsed suffix, in the explicitly limited view.

Preview yields an explicitly provisional view of current source. Finite-prefix
recovery in that view must not mutate the live delimiter/alternative continuation.
An open clean preview never authorizes execution. Finish may change diagnostics
without changing text: cache identity includes source revision AND interpretation
state/generation. Source revision alone cannot validate open/final cached output.

For x := "hel, the live string remains unfinished. Appending lo" completes it.
Only finish commits EOF recovery for any remaining unfinished construct. Errors
already established before the frontier still receive canonical S2 recovery.

3. Canonical continuation ownership
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Recognition (NoMatch/Match/Committed) remains separate from progress
(Continue/NeedInput/NeedsProcessing/Halted). Committed recovery is not suspension.
Internal frames retain owning rule and phase, source offset, delimiter/fence
ownership, alternatives and lookahead dependencies, scanner state, event/builder
state, and cumulative resources. A parent that would lose state on unwind needs
an explicit continuation, not a restart of the growing production.

Scanners retain escapes, partial delimiter matches, CRLF state, Unicode-sensitive
boundaries, and the examined frontier. Test :, :=, ., .., ..=, -, ->, ~, and ~>
as split prefixes using canonical selection rules. Long identifiers, strings,
comments, prose, and fenced bodies cannot rescan from their opening byte on each
append. A newline, closer, or successful prefix parse alone proves no universal
commitment boundary. Heading lookbehind, brace classification, and longer-token
alternatives retain their unresolved context. Replay is allowed only where its
bound is established and counted. Completed children may remain shared while
the enclosing document/section grows.

One-shot parsing must use this same recognition/recovery implementation with
final input. Frozen S7A fixtures are an independent regression reference in
addition to differential tests against the current one-shot entry point.

4. Source, tree, and publication ownership
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Preserve TextSnapshot identity, exact bytes, sharing, logical child order,
canonical shapes, and typed access. Appends must not copy all historical pieces,
scan old chunks for each range lookup, or rebuild the complete line index.
Do not normalize newlines/Unicode. Growing child arrays and structural hashes
also require bounded persistent updates, without artificial grammar nodes.

Ordinary updates publish progress, changed regions, and diagnostic deltas with a
shared/lazy provisional view. They must not enumerate every reused node or rebuild
all indexes. Full materialization, serialization, and explicitly requested whole
source/tree traversal are separate, visibly metered export operations. Merely
moving an unconditional full parse into ordinary preview does not meet the gate.

A non-append edit may invalidate continuations and use S7A's full canonical reparse.
Invalidate suspended frames and provisional caches explicitly; establish valid
streaming state before subsequent appends. Charge that restart and its reason.
Arbitrary edits need correctness and accounting, not a sublinear guarantee.

B2 storage checkpoint
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

TextSnapshot now stores pieces in a persistent ordered binary tree. Complete
power-of-two left subtrees bound append path copying and byte/chunk/range lookup
by tree depth. Sequential exports traverse the tree in linear time with a bounded
stack and no traversal allocation. Text equality still allocates no memory.
Line starts share the same storage mechanism; append scans only incoming bytes.
A CR/LF split replaces the final line-start path without modifying prior views.
Arbitrary edits may rebuild storage, then subsequent appends establish the exact
new line-ending frontier. Empty append retains the original source revision.

`TextSnapshot::append_with_work` reports new source bytes copied, new bytes scanned
for line indexing, tree nodes allocated, and their body bytes. Allocator headers
and caller-owned input construction are explicitly outside those byte fields.
An allocation-probe regression checks actual allocations against the node counts
and rejects historical-prefix copying through 16,384 retained pieces. The focused
`document_streaming_storage` target tests scaling with every historical snapshot
retained, as well as Unicode partitions and append/edit/append correctness.
These storage counters do not yet account for parser or publication work.

`LineIndex::line_starts` now explicitly exports a Vec rather than borrowing a flat
slice. Normal line lookup uses retained storage; full export pays for the returned
array. Source bytes, line order, typed syntax, and grammar inventory are unchanged.
This source-storage checkpoint does not make DocumentSession parsing resumable.

B2 Unicode scanner checkpoint
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Canonical cursor grapheme reads now use a retained Unicode segmentation cursor.
Open input retains an unfinished grapheme across appends, including unbounded
combining sequences. Each allowance unit supplies at most a forward scalar and
one preceding scalar (eight bytes) to the pinned Unicode implementation; requested
backward context is supplied one scalar per charged call. Bounded overlap keeps
regional-indicator state valid at chunk edges. Forward, lookbehind, and additional
context bytes are separately counted; source-tree lookup work still needs the
session-wide accounting introduced with the canonical continuation owner.

No Unicode classification tables or grammar rules are duplicated. Final one-shot
cursor reads exercise this implementation with final input; an open continuation
reports NeedInput or NeedsProcessing separately. Tests cover every scalar split
of CRLF, combining text, joined emoji, flags, and Indic conjuncts, plus one-step
allowances and long unfinished grapheme growth. This primitive is not yet a
retained string/identifier/fence parser: token phases, grammar frames, live events,
and efficient provisional publication remain required before B2-B4 closeout.

B2 literal scanner checkpoint
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Canonical exact-literal reads now retain both the expected and source Unicode
cursors, pending grapheme ranges, and byte-comparison offset. An allowance pays
for individual bounded Unicode calls and compared bytes; a long combined
literal cannot hide an unbounded expected-grapheme scan. The same scalar-only
adapter serves piece-backed source and borrowed literals without copying either.
Temporary input never completes an unresolved grapheme. Finalization is retained
before a cached result can return, so subsequent source growth is rejected.

Focused regressions compare every scalar cut and scalar-at-a-time input against
an independent contiguous Unicode iterator, including operator prefixes, CRLF,
combining marks, regional indicators, emoji joiners, and Indic sequences. They
also enforce one-unit polls, zero-work yields, invalid UTF-8 bounds, repeated
finish, and linear scanner work for growing long combined literals. Canonical
cursor reads use this scanner with final input; parent token/rule phases still
need conversion before ordinary document sessions can suspend on source input.

B3 parser-state ownership checkpoint
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

ParserState owns the event buffer, live markers, canonical rule stack, diagnostics,
covered range, nesting, remaining fuel, and resource-finalization state independently
of borrowed input and the ID generator. Ordinary one-shot construction/finalization
uses this same ownership boundary. Suspension moves the buffers; it does not clone,
finalize, rewind, or replenish them. Resume extends only explicit input-frontier
bounds. A fixed embedded range remains fixed even when its end coincided with the
previous source end; its separate outer context may continue growing.

Absolute diagnostic ranges in an accepted append-only prefix remain valid. Snapshot
export binds their revision while already visiting diagnostics, rather than scanning
all old diagnostics on every resume. Tests preserve diagnostic IDs, labels, buffer
identity, open markers/rules, and nonrefundable work across input growth. Edits must
invalidate this private live state; grammar frames and the public streaming owner
are still required before exposing resumable document parsing.

B3 canonical document-frame checkpoint
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The generated DocumentRule/GrammarExpression descriptions now execute through
owned rule entry/exit, sequence, choice/best-choice, optional/lookahead, repetition,
and separated-item phases. Each phase retains the original checkpoint, commitment,
selected alternative, fence state, marker/rule scope, and child position. Ordinary
one-shot document parsing drives this same implementation with final input. The
previous recursive combinator interpreter is removed, not retained as an alternate.

A scheduling allowance can yield between transitions without unwinding phases or
losing ParserState. Qualification resumes all 112 accepted document-rule witnesses
one transition at a time and compares their events and parser accounting with
uninterrupted execution. Focused cases additionally exercise zero-progress loops,
alternative selection, trailing separators, and hard-fuel recovery at every yield.
The new module participates in canonical parser isolation checks.

This checkpoint establishes grammar-phase ownership, not a finished input-stream
API. Token-specific phases, ordinary recursive-core calls, fence-body scanning,
resource/fairness accounting inside those calls, and temporary EOF handling still
need integration. The internal allowance counts document-frame transitions and converted child
work; it does not bound an unconverted ordinary child-rule call.

B2/B3 canonical base-rule phases
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The 149 canonical base-rule entries now run owned phases for fixed literals,
Unicode graphemes/classification, whitespace, identifiers/path segments, digit
sequences, alternatives, and escapes. Their former recursive driver is removed.
The existing fixed-terminal specification and base-rule selections remain the
recognition authority. Unicode escapes accumulate checked scalar values while
scanning rather than allocating and parsing the complete growing digit range.
Failed candidates still rewind to the canonical one-grapheme escape fallback.

Document frames retain base continuations and literal scans under the same
scheduling allowance. Completed scans publish tokens in separately scheduled
phases. Ordinary recursive-core rules and other unconverted document children
still need conversion; this checkpoint does not expose a document stream API.

Tests split base-rule sources at every scalar boundary and into scalar chunks,
yield after each unit of scanner/frame work, and compare events, consumed bytes,
and parser resources across fuel budgets. Once fuel is exhausted, the input owner
stops accepting chunks: the Limited result retains open owners before resource
finalization, then draining sealed input matches one-shot parsing of that exact
accepted prefix. Repeated limited polls neither advance nor refund work. Growing
identifiers, whitespace, and Unicode escape digits retain linear scanner/frame
work at N, 2N, 4N, and 8N. These counters still exclude storage-index traversal and
publication; the end-to-end B1 performance gates remain required and failing.

B2/B3 string candidate and recovery phases
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Raw and UTF-8 strings now retain opening/closing quote counts, base-rule body
continuations, delimiter probes, candidate checkpoints, markers, and recovery
phases. The ordinary string entry points use this same execution path. An open
raw candidate remains pending until success or a stable failure; only then may
the STRING owner select its canonical UTF-8 candidate. Final EOF runs the existing
rule-owned missing-closer diagnostics and opening labels. Recovery may replay a
failed final candidate once; that scanner/frame work is counted, not refunded.

Every scalar cut and scalar-at-a-time tests compare events, diagnostic content,
consumed bytes, and parser resources, including incomplete triple delimiters,
Unicode/CRLF bodies, malformed escapes, and hard-fuel accepted-prefix outcomes.
N, 2N, 4N, and 8N tests include final candidate replay for growing closed/unclosed
bodies. Document frames retain direct string owners under their shared allowance;
strings reached through an unconverted recursive-core parent still require that
parent's owned continuation before document append can suspend through it.

The repository corpus inventory records this design document as a planning
artifact under the same canonical-specification policy as the continuation plan.
It is not a raw-parser fixture. Existing source fixtures and all four failing
positive end-to-end streaming acceptance cases remain in their original gates.

B2/B3 comment and paragraph phases
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Comments retain leading spacing, the canonical two-spelling sigil selection,
and raw ANY_TOKEN body children until a physical newline or final EOF. Paragraph
text retains exact exclusion probes, its definition-operator lookahead, and TEXT
child continuations. Both ordinary entry points execute the retained phases;
the former growing loops are removed. A proven definition-lookahead whitespace
range is shared across subsequent TEXT children, so consuming a long settled
space run does not rescan the remainder from every character. Open lookahead
retains its inspected frontier and waits for enough input to decide :=.

Every scalar cut and scalar chunks compare exact events, normalized diagnostic
content, consumed source, and resource outcomes. N through 8N tests cover growing
comments, leading comment spacing, and positive/negative/end-of-input definition
lookahead after long whitespace, counting both append and one-shot work. Direct
Document child phases retain these continuations under their common allowance.
Other Mechdown and recursive-core parent conversions remain required.

B2/B3 fence scanner and embedded-scope phases
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Fence delimiter search retains its literal probes and Unicode traversal across
input frontiers and bounded work yields. Document frames own the scan checkpoint,
charged grapheme advances, bounded MECH_CODE child, fallback/recovery selection,
and cursor restoration. The previous recursive fence helper and borrowed cursor
closure are removed. Borrow-free scope records restore fixed enclosing bounds or
the current source frontier correctly after suspension/append, including resource
remainders whose physical cursor extends beyond an embedded consume bound.

Delimiter tests compare every scalar partition with independent contiguous
Unicode search and measure N through 8N unfinished bodies/combined graphemes.
Existing one-shot document/fence/recovery behavior still uses delimiter discovery
before bounded body interpretation. Efficient finite-prefix preview of an open
fence requires retained body interpretation/publication work in B4; this scanner
checkpoint alone does not qualify ordinary previews or end-to-end streaming.

B3 operator continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

All 53 canonical expression-operator rules now retain their ordered alternatives,
node markers, leading/trailing spacing, and negative lookahead checkpoints.
Comment-sigil, matrix-multiply, and generator-arrow guards retain their child
continuations without refunding probe work. Literal operator atoms retain Unicode
boundary checks under the same allowance. Ordinary operator entry points drain
these same phases; the former synchronous operator helpers are removed.

Direct document children own the operator continuation. Qualification covers every
operator rule and spelling, overlapping prefixes, Unicode spacing and combining
marks, every scalar cut, scalar chunks, and hard-fuel outcomes. N through 8N
leading/trailing spacing tests require linear work for both incremental and
one-shot execution. Recursive expression parents still require retained phases;
this operator conversion does not yet provide an end-to-end document stream.

B3 context-path and primitive-kind continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Context path tokens, repeated paths, @context/path prefixes, and primitive
any/empty/atom kinds retain their token choices, prefix stages, and repetitions.
Ordinary entry points and direct document children use those same continuations.
Unicode identifiers, incomplete prefixes, repeated underscores, input partitions,
and per-call yields share the base scanner and cumulative parser fuel.

Failed candidates let their transaction discard provisional markers. This also
handles a child that already finalized a hard-limit source remainder: rejecting
an enclosing incomplete context prefix preserves the child/remainder instead of
attempting to abandon a resource-finalizing marker. Direct public prefix tests
cover fuel 0 through 64 and four event capacities; resumed tests compare exact
accepted-prefix events, diagnostics, and resource outcomes. Growing context names,
paths, primitive atom names, and underscore kinds have N through 8N work gates.

B3 Mechdown leaf continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The remaining ten closed Mechdown leaves retain codeblock sigil selection, fence
rejection for inline code, hyperlink prefix probes, inline/block body children,
reference alternatives, line whitespace, and final recovery. Comment and prose
owners remain shared with their existing retained phases. Ordinary entry points
and document child frames drain the same implementation. There is no second
streaming grammar or fallback to the removed synchronous body loops.

Literal delimiter probes and base children yield under the shared allowance.
Temporary input exhaustion retains the live body instead of inserting closing
syntax or missing-content diagnostics. Physical newline boundaries still trigger
the same canonical recovery, and line rules still require a physical newline.
All scalar partitions and low-fuel cases preserve canonical events/diagnostics;
N through 8N gates cover open/closed bodies, references, and growing line spacing.
These leaf guarantees do not yet qualify ordinary document previews or the
remaining recursive expression parents.

B3 numeric and primitive-literal continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

All 21 non-string literal entries retain ordered candidates, optional signs,
scientific and imaginary markers, typed suffixes, based-number payloads, and
candidate-specific recovery policy. A complex-number candidate retains its
nonrecovering untyped-real children; only the canonical selected real-number
owner may insert missing based payloads. Direct string entries continue to use
the existing retained string owner. The former recursive numeric driver and
its separate candidate helpers are removed.

Ordinary and document-child parsing use the same phases. Input-cut and low-fuel
qualification covers every entry, including late suffixes, invalid payloads,
Unicode identifiers/digits, and failed complex candidates. N through 8N work
gates include final candidate replay, long numeric payloads, typed identifiers,
empty literals, and atoms, with complete accepted source and no resource caps.
This qualifies these leaf continuations, not end-to-end document publication.

B3 closed control, pattern, and subscript continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The fifteen closed control/pattern/subscript rules use shared retained primitive
phases for spacing, ordered assignment choices, transparent terminals, wildcard
and spread selection, identifier/integer subscripts, and repeated swizzle tails.
Each comma-plus-identifier swizzle tail owns its checkpoint until it either
completes or leaves the physical comma for its enclosing grammar owner. Integer
subscripts own the retained numeric continuation under the same work allowance.
The original synchronous primitive bodies are removed.

Partition/resource tests cover all fifteen rules, Unicode identifiers, split
operators/CRLF, and incomplete swizzle tails. N through 8N gates exercise growing
swizzles, identifiers, integers, and control whitespace, preserving complete
source and the specified trailing-comma ownership. Recursive statement, pattern,
and subscript parents remain separate continuation work.

B3 structure-shell continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The ten closed structure-shell rules retain matrix/table delimiter choices,
table separator spacing, physical-newline table tops, row-border lookahead and
space runs, and empty map/set children. Repeated border items retain their
checkpoints and base children; an optional empty-set marker uses the numeric
literal continuation under the same allowance. Ordinary and direct document
entry points use these phases, replacing the synchronous shell loops.

All scalar cuts and low-fuel outcomes cover round/square/bold box delimiters,
separator lookahead across long spaces, split CRLF, combining characters, and
incomplete empty collections. N through 8N gates include both successful and
failed table tops, row space lookahead, borders, and empty collection contents.
The complete matrix/table/map/set owners still require recursive continuations.

B3 declaration continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The eight export/context declaration rules retain URI alternatives, capability
path tokens, wildcard validation, and optional capability-group checkpoints.
Path validation visits one byte per phase without copying the candidate text.
A group keeps its separator and whole-group rollback boundaries across yields;
incomplete or invalid suffixes preserve the canonical declaration prefix.
Ordinary and direct document entry points drain the same retained phases.

All input cuts and low-fuel outcomes cover the eight rules, URI prefixes,
Unicode and CRLF boundaries, wildcard placement, and group rollback. N through
8N gates cover long names, spacing, URI components, valid and invalid paths,
and complete or rejected capability groups. These tests compare complete
accepted source, events, diagnostics, consumption, and parser resource stats.
Import and recursive-core continuations remain unfinished B3 work.

B3 source-import continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

All thirteen source-import rules retain ordered relative/absolute/URI/bare
selection, component and URI-tail scanning, slash-pair rollback, and optional
wildcard suffixes. The maximal file-path check visits one byte per phase;
declaration wildcard validation visits one scalar per phase and builds physical
wildcard labels incrementally. Neither check copies the whole candidate text.
Unicode trailing whitespace is trimmed only for wildcard validation, preserving
the syntax range and exact diagnostic anchors. Resource finalization discards
unselected wrappers while retaining their finalized children and source.

All cuts and low-fuel tests cover the thirteen rules. N through 8N gates cover
paths, URI tails and schemes, ordered fallback, Unicode trailing whitespace, and
multiple wildcard labels. Public regressions check exact Unicode ranges and
lossless results across fuel/event limits. Module-import and recursive-core
owners, shared recovery scheduling, and complete document EOF remain B3 work.

B3 shared error-skip and physical context probes
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Shared skip-error recovery now owns scalar consumption, byte-limit decisions,
error markers, fence/subtitle lookahead, and found-text materialization across
appends and work yields. Ordinary recovery drains this same implementation.
Physical context boundary helpers likewise drain the shared resumable probes;
the prior synchronous context-scanning bodies are removed. A failed fence probe
retains the indentation range it ruled out, avoiding repeated scans from each
following space. Error text is materialized one scalar per phase.

Partition tests cover all three recovery classes, split CRLF and fence prefixes,
subtitle decisions, exact stop offsets, and diagnostic content. Recovery-byte
and event limits remain cumulative. N through 8N gates cover indentation,
subtitle lookahead, and Unicode error text. These are phase-work checks;
complete storage/export accounting remains B5 work.

B3 module-import continuations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

All nineteen module-import rules retain intrinsic/name selection, alias paths,
transactional separator/item pairs, group commitment, required-target recovery,
and the top-level context-alias recovery path. The invalid slash continuation
uses the shared resumable skip-error owner. Direct and document entry points
share these phases; the former synchronous module-import bodies are removed.

Input-cut and low-fuel tests cover every rule, incomplete pairs, local recovery,
Unicode and CRLF, and malformed context aliases. N through 8N gates cover paths,
groups, alias operators, ordered fallback, and context-alias error tails. Public
regressions preserve lossless trees across fuel/event exhaustion inside nested
recovery owners.

B3 physical found-syntax and missing-node recovery
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Physical found-syntax classification now retains the shared terminal-table
iteration, literal and Unicode scanners, longest-match selection, and scalar
text export. Ordinary physical classification drains that same owner. Shared
missing-node recovery retains marker completion, classification, and diagnostic
publication; module imports use it under the same scheduling allowance. A fixed
non-name with sufficient physical lookahead can recover before final EOF.

All fixed-terminal spellings and Unicode input cuts compare exact found syntax.
N through 8N tests cover long combining and ZWJ clusters including text export.
Module-import partition and resource regressions pass through the retained
missing owner, and an explicit open-input regression prevents final-EOF gating
from returning to physical missing-name recovery.

Filtered grammar diagnostic classification retains its separate lexical
contract and still drains at final input. Its continuation, recursive-core
owners, the remaining recovery routines, and complete document EOF scheduling
remain unfinished B3 work.

B3 precedence-phase ownership
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The seven precedence levels now retain their transaction, marker, selected
operator, pair count, operand boundary, and commitment across work yields.
Seeded formulas drain the same level owner, including conditional chain nodes
and completion of remaining outer markers after resource exhaustion. Operator
selection uses the existing retained operators and preserves the level-four
multiply/divide then matrix-operator ordering. The synchronous level loops are
removed. Operator-restart recovery preserves its selected operator and rejected
trivia lookahead policy.

Scheduling tests compare all seven direct levels across input partitions and
low fuel. Factor bodies and operand-restart recovery are still synchronous
children and wait for final input; their internal work is not bounded by these
precedence phase counters. This is recursive-core ownership groundwork, not
qualification of streaming expressions. Those children, the rest of the
recursive core, and document EOF scheduling remain B3 implementation work.

5. Limits and deterministic accounting
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Per-call allowance yields NeedsProcessing and preserves resumable state.
Hard session limits cap retained bytes, nesting/frames, events, diagnostics,
recovery work, and total work. Chunk boundaries do not reset these limits;
rewinding speculative alternatives never refunds work. Preview/export work is
separately attributed AND included in total charged work. Repeated provisional
recovery cannot escape metering. Saturation cannot silently wrap a counter.
Hard exhaustion is Limited, never NeedInput, and cannot discard accepted source.

Instrument at the owning operation, not by inferring work from reused IDs:

- accepted source bytes; scanner/parser steps; replayed bytes/steps;
- continuation resumes; emitted events; changed tree elements;
- source and child-array bytes copied; source/index maintenance work;
- diagnostic and ordinary publication work; preview/export work;
- full-document restart count and explicit reasons;
- peak live continuation/storage usage, separate from historical snapshots.

No-limit final results must agree across streamed and one-shot execution.
At limits, require the documented bounded, lossless result and correct reporting;
different strategies need not exhaust fuel at the same byte or have equal costs.

6. B1 baseline and performance gates
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The S7A DocumentSession always calls full canonical reparse for nonempty edits.
TextSnapshot append copies the piece descriptors; range lookup walks pieces.
Reparse builds fresh syntax/indexes and reconciles the old and new trees.
The baseline driver in document_streaming_complexity exercises that real API;
it is test-only and is not a proposed streaming wrapper or implementation.

The B1 counters are PARTIAL ACCOUNTING: parser steps, events, reserved
reconciliation allowance/work, and full-document restarts exposed by S7A.
Reconciliation includes reservations, so their sum is not an exact measurement
or a lower bound on executed CPU instructions.
Source copying, scanner internals, index maintenance, and exports are not fully
instrumented yet. Do not claim end-to-end cost from these counters. B2-B4 must
replace the driver with the real lifecycle and complete the owner-level metrics.
The positive acceptance assertions intentionally fail on this S7A baseline.
No ignored tests or special passing baseline mode qualify streaming.

Test fixed chunk sizes at N, 2N, 4N, 8N for a long unfinished token, growing nested
Mech expression, and fenced body. Compare each doubling with a <=3x work bound,
allowing linear/logarithmic overhead but rejecting repeated-prefix quadratic cost.
Audit both ingestion and ingestion plus normal view publication. Test one small
append to increasingly large settled prefixes with a separately bounded cost.
All tests must verify complete accepted source, final canonical structure and
normalized diagnostics, and absence of fuel/event/recovery/diagnostic truncation.
Explicit export is measured separately. Timings support, but do not replace,
deterministic counters. These selected workload bounds are not a universal
linear-time claim about every canonical grammar/input combination.

Measured B1 baseline (nightly-2026-03-03, locked/offline, no default features):

| Family | N=64 | N=128 | N=256 | N=512 |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| string | 8910 | 23214 | 68718 | 227310 |
| nested | 33036 | 86300 | 256572 | 852092 |
| fence | 8627 | 22505 | 67757 | 228245 |
| settled | 25303 | 50455 | 100759 | 201367 |

Values sum the three exposed accounting counters, including reconciliation
reservations; they are not elapsed time or executed instruction counts. Ingestion-only and
normal-view totals agree because S7A eagerly constructs the snapshot during edits.
The settled case appends six bytes to N repeated paragraphs. All four positive
performance gates fail after completing source/equivalence and cap checks.
The exact sample/counter record is `s7b-streaming-baseline.json`. B2-B4 must add
missing accounting; this table does not certify any streaming implementation.

7. Qualification and internal checkpoints
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The single S7B PR uses these six canonical commits. While a checkpoint remains
in progress, implementation fixes amend that commit. Later checkpoints receive
commits when their deliverables exist; commit presence alone is not closeout.

B1 — Contract and baseline: document lifecycle, provisional/final behavior,
scope, metrics, and failing streaming-performance tests against S7A.
B2 — Append storage and scanners: efficient source append, resumable lexical
scanning, boundary tests, and accurate counters.
B3 — Canonical continuations: grammar suspension/resumption, alternative
ownership, final EOF handling, and shared recovery integration.
B4 — Snapshots and sessions: efficient normal publication, diagnostic deltas,
identity handling, previews, and edit/stream transitions.
B5 — Complete qualification: partition tests, malformed/resource tests,
adversarial complexity, typed-consumer canaries, and CI execution.
B6 — Closeout and S8 handoff: exact-head results, API documentation, supported
performance claims, and production integration instructions.

Begin B2/B3 with the three different unfinished families, not only independent
terminated statements. Keep all checkpoints in this single draft PR.

Focused integration targets:

- document_streaming_lifecycle: empty append, work yield, repeat finish,
  terminal API errors, cancellation, and finality/cache transitions;
- document_streaming_equivalence: tree/tokens/flags/losslessness, normalized
  diagnostic fields, typed roles, and supported semantic consumer canaries;
- document_streaming_boundaries: operators, strings/escapes, CRLF, graphemes,
  headings/fences, comprehensions, brace/shared prefixes, late disambiguation;
- document_streaming_recovery: provisional vs live state, established errors,
  physical closer ownership, later children, and canonical final EOF recovery;
- document_streaming_resources: every hard limit, resumable allowances,
  repeated previews, accepted suffix preservation, and suspended cancellation;
- document_streaming_complexity: deterministic cumulative gates described above;
- document_incremental: append/edit/append, identity and annotation invalidation.

Short fixtures use every UTF-8 character-boundary split and selected multipart
partitions; long fixtures use deterministic random, character, line, and large
chunks. Include combining characters and joined emoji. A test-only byte adapter
buffers incomplete UTF-8 suffixes and rejects malformed bytes, exercising every
byte split without transporting bytes inside the parser. Preview tests compare
the finite-prefix canonical result AND ensure the eventual final result is
unchanged. Ignore generated IDs/English wording in structural comparisons;
verify identity continuity separately.

CI's full/base mech-syntax --tests commands execute new integration targets.
Reduced-feature explicit streaming targets are added as they exist; --lib alone
is insufficient. Run pinned nightly-2026-03-03 with locked dependencies, explicit
grammar, reduced/no-std, architecture/generator, affected native/WASM, and complete
accumulated-stack consumers. Attribute results to exact heads/merge candidates.
Do not refresh grammar rows, generated files, or certification hashes for naming.

B3 recursive atom and recovery ownership

Formula, factor, unary, literal, variable, and annotation-prefix entry points now
drain retained owners in ordinary parsing as well. Ordered literal children,
variable candidate/comparison rollback, factor stem selection, unary nesting,
and transpose suffixes retain their marker/transaction state across scheduling.
The nested structure/call/slice and kind-interior children still require final
input; these are explicit remaining B3 work, not qualified streaming families.

Balanced abandonment now owns its delimiter stack, ordinary/raw quote state,
escapes, canonical annotation lookahead, and incremental found-text export.
Required-production and closer recovery share this owner and missing-node
publication. Operator restart probes retain their child continuation, checkpoint,
last result, and proven non-operator trivia range. The synchronous abandonment
and required-production implementations were removed. Closing-set callbacks,
nesting-limit scanning, filtered found classification, and full document EOF
scheduling remain to be converted.

New all-cut and one-unit scheduling regressions cover recursive atoms, balanced
recovery, required-production lookahead, low fuel, and cumulative recovery/event
limits. N/2N/4N/8N recovery tests include scanning and diagnostic text export.
A nested-expression stack overflow exposed an oversized inline recovery child;
that child is now heap-owned and the unchanged nested-complexity test passes.
These checks do not replace B5's complete end-to-end publication qualification.

B3 recursive kind and nesting-recovery ownership

All eleven recursive kind entries now share retained owners. Ordered primitive
choice, annotation candidates, optional suffixes, matrix cardinality, tuple and
table fields, and shared brace record/map/set selection retain child state and
rollback points. Parameterized TAG matching uses the shared retained literal
scanner. A scalar-kind range still delegates to the unconverted range parent;
this remaining child prevents claiming full recursive-family qualification.

Nesting-limit recovery retains its parentheses depth, comment-prefix checks,
subtitle/fence context probes, missing-node publication, and skipped-text export.
Ordinary parsing drains the same owner; no synchronous nesting scanner remains.
All-cut tests cover source, fuel, recovery/event allowances, and error boundaries.
N/2N/4N/8N kind-list, nested-kind, and nesting-recovery cases consume the complete
source and include their retained scanner/export work. They do not establish
B4's normal snapshot-publication complexity or complete B5 qualification.

B3 range and structure-prefix ownership

Range expressions retain their initial formula, both operator/bound pairs,
required-bound recovery, and transaction. Parenthetical terms retain their
opening, nested formula, whitespace, closer, and shared recovery. Scalar-kind
ranges now call this owner rather than a final-input body.

Table alternatives, their physical opening prefixes, record openers, and matrix
openers now retain canonical wrappers and discriminator facts. Ordinary table,
record, and matrix entry points drain the same prefix owners. Their interiors
and the other structure-selection bodies remain explicit unfinished B3 children.
This lets ordinary scalar factors reject unrelated structure alternatives and
advance long formula chains before final EOF. A cursor-progress regression
verifies this behavior directly; scalar formula/string/number N/2N/4N/8N tests
check retained work while consuming the complete source.

The recursive dispatcher outlines range/parenthetical transitions so additional
state does not enlarge unrelated nested call paths. The unchanged native nested
complexity regression passes. Focused qualification for this checkpoint contains
370 tests across 25 targets, plus no-std and architecture/generator checks.

B3 expression and postfix ownership

Expressions retain formula/range/match selection and discriminator facts. Calls,
bound arguments, argument lists (including FSM arguments), slices, and subscript
lists retain children, separators, nesting, and required-value/closer recovery.
Expression range bounds share the range owner with direct range expressions.
An established low-budget rejected bound-argument case (`x+1`, fuel 1) now lets
its transaction discard provisional markers after child resource finalization.

Open-input regressions verify cursor progress through completed operands,
arguments, and indices. Long N/2N/4N/8N scalar expression/call/slice cases include
retained grammar work; shorter separate cursor checks isolate temporary-EOF
behavior. Explicit structure-expression selection and match/FSM-value bodies
still contain final-input children. Full document EOF scheduling and B4–B6 remain
unfinished; these local results do not establish end-to-end streaming acceptance.

8. Closeout and S8 handoff
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Keep S7B open until correctness, actual resumability, efficient full update cost,
explicit lifecycle/resource behavior, architecture preservation, and observed
final-head qualification all pass. Known failing acceptance cannot be relabelled.

S8 uses append/advance for arriving text, provisional views for tools, and finish
at the consumer's explicit completion boundary. Only finalized validated syntax
is handed to semantic consumers. Production migration/removal stays in S8.

B3 pattern, qualifier, and collection ownership
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Definitions retain the physically recognized definition-operator fact. FSM pipes,
instances, transitions, and argument lists share the recursive owners. Patterns
retain wildcard and spread/rest facts across nested children; array validation
folds those facts and token cardinality into constant-size state instead of
collecting and rescanning a token list. FSM value exclusion consumes those facts.
Match arms retain optional guard candidates and required output recovery.
Comprehension qualifiers preserve actual generator/let recognition independently
of recovery, including a missing source after a physically recognized arrow.

Tuple/set bodies, parenthesis selection, bindings, mappings, and record bodies
now retain their children and recovery phases. A parenthesis candidate keeps its
first expression while choosing tuple or parenthetical roles. Binding candidates
retain value checkpoints for the existing clean-subtree reuse path; mapping
lookahead retains quotes, raw triples, delimiters, and annotation probes. Shared
closer recovery supports canonical table/matrix shells as well as base tokens.
Table headers and ordinary/framed row owners retain separator candidates and
empty-row recovery. Their enclosing table bodies remain the next conversion.

Ordinary entry points drain these same owners. Obsolete synchronous bodies and
fact/recovery adapters were removed as their last callers moved. Input-cut tests
cover clean, malformed, and resource-limited paths. N/2N/4N/8N owner tests cover
growing pattern arrays, tuples, mapping lists, parenthesized formulas, and binding
strings. These are owner-level results, not the four end-to-end publication gates.
The shared dispatcher passes boxed phases without unpacking them on unrelated
recursive paths, and lexical children are boxed. The unchanged nested complexity
test passes without increasing its thread-stack limit.

B3 document-frontier and recursive ownership checkpoint
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Every frozen Phase 2I rule now has a canonical continuation. Shared bracket,
brace, inline-table, matrix-row, and table-body selection retains the same
alternative and recovery policy as ordinary parsing. No final-only recursive
child bridge remains. The isolation inventory covers every moved owner module.

Document combinators accept open input and retain Mika literal parts, leading
comment probes, required items, missing fence closers, nesting recovery, root
fallback, and abandonment. The executable-fence delimiter scanner feeds known
safe prefixes into a retained Mech-code child; only a found closer or final input
seals that child. Header classification scans a bounded prefix under its allowance
and shares CodeFenceInfo's language-prefix table. Filtered grammar diagnostics
feed the same found-syntax classifier after incremental scalar filtering.
Resource diagnostic classification is deferred into a retained child rather than
performing a potentially long grapheme scan inside marker completion.

The full library and the document fence/incremental/isolation targets pass
199 tests at this ownership checkpoint. Earlier all-recursive qualification
passed 380 tests across 25 targets. Arbitrary document cuts include executable
and inert fences, malformed inline code, comments, headings, and Mika, with
one-transition suspension and low fuel. Filtered diagnostic cuts separately
exercise ignored trivia inside operators, combining clusters, and joined emoji.
These are ownership results, not end-to-end streaming qualification. B4 must
replace eager publication and account for retained tree/cache materialization;
B5 must run the final full matrix and turn all four B1 performance gates green.

B4 snapshots and sessions checkpoint
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

DocumentStream::new/with_limits starts an open canonical document. append and
advance return NeedInput or NeedsProcessing separately from Finished, Cancelled,
and Limited. finish declares final EOF and is idempotent; cancel preserves source.
Oversized appends reject atomically. Empty appends preserve identity, counters,
and outstanding scheduling status. Hard parser work remains cumulative.

StreamUpdate carries compact replacement suffixes for event and diagnostic
journals. StreamView shares those persistent journals and the source, exposes
accepted/pending ranges, and supplies existing SyntaxNode values for materialized
completed markers. Looking up a completed node uses the event index; it does not
rebuild NodeIndex or enumerate unchanged nodes. Abandoned speculative markers
are removed from the current journal while older views remain immutable.

Completed markers own immutable green nodes with stable identities. Retained
materialization hashes token bytes under the continuation allowance and reuses
completed children. Parent child storage copies logarithmic tree paths; child
order and the frozen Phase 2I-C structural hashes are unchanged. Typed child
iteration is lazy. Clean brace/map replay consumes the same cached subtree rather
than synchronously sinking its event range again.

preview explicitly runs canonical finite-prefix interpretation, separately
charged, without changing the live grammar, fuel, or recovery. Preview identities
are distinct from live/final identities even at the same revision. Preview IDs
come from the session sequence, preventing element-ID collisions with live nodes.
materialize explicitly exports the finalized or limited tree and indexes once;
repeated calls share the result. A preview or limited result never authorizes
execution. S8 must require Finished/Finalized and normal strict validation.

apply_edits discards suspended frames and materialization work, invalidates all
identities in the old live interpretation, and charges a full restart. Historical
views remain valid. Subsequent appends resume the new interpretation. Existing
DocumentSession ordinary edits preserve their established reconciliation policy;
into_stream establishes retained parsing, and into_session explicitly exports a
finalized/limited snapshot for editing. Production callers remain unchanged.

StreamWork separates accepted/copied/indexed source, persistent allocation and
mutation work, canonical continuation/scanner/materialization work, checkpoint
rewinds and reused bytes, normal publications, previews, explicit exports, and
edit restarts. It records component peaks for source pieces, events, markers,
rule depth, document frames, and pending materialization requests. Event/node
storage and materialization belong to normal processing, not hidden preview.
Full export charges a conservative volume including source, events, diagnostics,
node/token indexes, restarts, and any remaining resource cleanup. Arbitrary edit
storage work has a documented linear/logarithmic bound separate from measured
append counters; it is not covered by the small-append performance claim.

Focused B4 qualification passes 26 tests across lifecycle, equivalence, resources,
complexity, certification, and frozen rule-surface targets. The four original
positive gates now use DocumentStream, include ordinary publication and final
canonical draining, and retain full-source/uncapped/equivalence checks. A broad
full run passed 890 tests and surfaced two storage-refactor issues (the canonical
type allowlist and frozen hash preservation); both pass focused reruns. The
165-test library and existing typed/incremental targets also pass. Final exact-head
base/full, reduced/native/WASM, consumer, review, and CI results remain B5/B6 work.

B5 complete qualification implementation
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The boundary/recovery/resource suites now exercise byte transport partitions,
random long partitions, preview isolation, physical closers, accepted suffixes,
and session transitions. Existing semantic/artifact consumers have finalized
stream canaries. Full CI explicitly includes all streaming targets in the reduced
syntax profile and the semantic canary in the full_source producer profile.

Adversarial growth includes combining clusters, regional indicators, executable
fence lines, malformed tails, and late brace selection. Tests retain historical
normal views and exercise bounded completed-node access; final grammar draining
is included before the separate explicit export. Source lookup counters count
actual retained-tree visits on the private parser source; public reads cannot
mutate these counters. Sequential base and delimiter scans retain Unicode cursor
state. Literal prefix rejection avoids rescanning nonmatching regional-indicator
context; ASCII frontier probes still wait for complete grapheme context.

Five B4 review regressions cover pre-allocation edit capacity rejection, cumulative
live plus preview parser allowance, limited-export identity/publication baselines,
initial session storage gauges, and diagnostic/restart/payload clone accounting.
Preview parser transitions share max_parser_work with live transitions. Preview
and resource-envelope export remain separately attributed in total work.

This checkpoint installs the complete qualification surface. Full/base, reduced,
no-std/WASM and CI outcomes must be recorded at their exact heads before B6 can
close the PR's implementation review; test presence is not a passing result.
